{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>An ox or a sheep or a goat.</b> They are called by their ending form, like \"and you shall strip off the garments of the naked\"; \"the dead shall be put to death,\" \"when the falling one falls.\" Or the reason is a mention of the species." "And the meaning of <b>and from the eighth day.</b> Like the circumcised one, until the quarter." "<b>And onward.</b> After it. And the witness is the arrow of Jonathan."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "The first two examples illustrate Ibn Ezra's point that words can be named or read by their final form rather than initial; the third example involves singular/plural variation. The argument is compressed and remains so.", 1 "The referent of 'the quarter' (המרובע) is cryptic and left untranslated literally per discipline.", 2 "Hyper-literal; 'the arrow of Jonathan' (חץ יהונתן) is a cryptic cross-reference, preserved as-is."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:11:47.828219576Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}